1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,810 --> 00:00:07,150
(Episode 29)

4
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:13,350
Hey.

5
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:15,950
Why are you here?

6
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,860
Right, you are unemployed now.

7
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:21,490
Goodness.

8
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,860
Why haven't you gone
to the restaurant yet?

9
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,670
Let's hurry before Mrs. Choi
gives us an earful again.

10
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,540
Goodness, Mi Mi.

11
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:35,940
Why do you keep carrying around
that closed savings bankbook?

12
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:41,110
What do you mean
you closed a savings account?

13
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:45,220
Mom, what is she talking about?

14
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:47,550
Da Mi.

15
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:51,220
Well, you see,

16
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:54,460
I saw the bankbook last night
before bed,

17
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,160
and I had to ask her about it.

18
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:59,960
The truth is, the money
your mom saved for your wedding...

19
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,030
Ri Ja.

20
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:05,170
Go ahead and get
the restaurant ready. Hurry.

21
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:06,640
All right.

22
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,810
Anyway, it is no big deal.

23
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:12,040
Don't make such a big fuss over it.

24
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,190
Let's sit down for a second.

25
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:26,420
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

26
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:34,230
I really have no pride.

27
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,400
Even if he is my son,
I kicked him out...

28
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,610
and put all my assets
in my daughter-in-law's name.

29
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:43,580
What do I expect
to gain at my age...

30
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:47,110
by constantly bringing over
kimchi and side dishes?

31
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,950
If Mi Mi finds out about this,
what will she say to me?

32
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:56,450
- Did you say something, Mrs. Choi?
- Goodness! You scared me.

33
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:59,360
Make some noise when you walk in.

34
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,760
Do you know you've been
so on edge lately?

35
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:06,500
Why is Mi Mi not here yet?

36
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,300
Well, you know about...

37
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:13,770
that savings account
she opened for Da Mi, right?

38
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:17,110
- What about it?
- She closed it.

39
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,850
She ended up doing it after all.

40
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:25,480
It's obvious where that money
ended up going.

41
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:29,650
And on top of that,
Da Mi found out about it.

42
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,430
How did Da Mi find out?

43
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:38,160
Unless someone told her
straight to her face,

44
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,430
how could she know?

45
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,500
I know, right?

46
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,870
How did she find out?

47
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,710
It is just as your aunt said.

48
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:56,810
I saved it for over 20 years...

49
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:59,450
to give to you when you got married,

50
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,450
but I closed it recently.

51
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:06,260
Why?

52
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,330
I helped your brother.

53
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:13,530
Which one this time?

54
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,600
The second one?

55
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,200
Yes.

56
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:21,510
You saved up 80,000 dollars?

57
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:28,980
You scrimped and saved for 20 years,
penny by penny, just for me.

58
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:35,050
Are you saying you broke into that
and gave it to him...

59
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,620
to help pay off his debts?

60
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,890
I did not give it away.
I lent it to him.

61
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,560
I made that very clear.

62
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,660
Dae Chi will definitely pay it back.

63
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:47,170
You know he is capable of that.

64
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,700
He has a stable job,

65
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,770
so he will be back on his feet
in a few years.

66
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:55,740
You should've at least told me.

67
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,180
Da Mi...

68
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:02,780
Sweetheart.

69
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:04,050
You...

70
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,420
should've talked to me first, Mom.

71
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:11,560
I meant to.

72
00:04:12,590 --> 00:04:14,360
I really wanted to,

73
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,500
but I just couldn't bring myself
to say it.

74
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:30,540
Then you shouldn't have
asked me how much I'd saved.

75
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:33,010
What?

76
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:35,950
Da Mi...

77
00:04:55,970 --> 00:04:58,470
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

78
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,940
Why am I crying?

79
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,480
It was Mom's money anyway, not mine.

80
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,590
Seriously.

81
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:30,170
Welcome, Seung Yun.

82
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,440
I must've surprised you.

83
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,070
I'm sorry to bother you so early,
Dr. Ju.

84
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:37,440
Not at all. I figured
you would come back,

85
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:41,380
since you left
without getting an answer from me.

86
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:43,950
That's a relief.

87
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:46,780
I brought warm drinks.
Would that be all right?

88
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:49,220
Of course. Please, have a seat.

89
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:51,990
Come in.

90
00:05:53,730 --> 00:05:55,730
Our guest brought cake, Director.

91
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,260
You didn't have to bring anything.

92
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,970
It is nothing, really.

93
00:06:01,370 --> 00:06:02,870
I just didn't want to show up
empty-handed.

94
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,300
Thank you.

95
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:06,670
You are welcome.

96
00:06:07,410 --> 00:06:10,640
Clinic hours haven't started yet,
so take your time.

97
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,710
- Okay.
- Thank you.

98
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:21,550
I won't leave
without an answer today.

99
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,350
Please, tell me.

100
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,160
It is not a very pleasant story.

101
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,200
When you actually hear it,

102
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:37,070
it might sound trivial
and underwhelming.

103
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,640
Even so, I want to hear it.

104
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:48,580
It was back when I was working...

105
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:50,350
at a university hospital
in the countryside.

106
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,690
Yes, come in.

107
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:06,600
Dad! Dad, I want strawberry.

108
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,870
- What about you? Chocolate?
- What?

109
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,670
Ju Ni kept begging me,
so we are going to buy cake.

110
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:13,940
You want some too, right?

111
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:17,510
I was actually craving
something sweet,

112
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:19,740
but how are you getting to the cafe?

113
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,510
The car is in the shop.

114
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:25,780
We can just walk.
It will be good exercise.

115
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,690
Aren't you coming with us, Dad?

116
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,260
Come with us, okay?

117
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:35,430
I'm sorry, sweetie.

118
00:07:35,630 --> 00:07:38,060
Daddy has so much to prepare
for his presentation right now.

119
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,430
I will go with you next time.

120
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:44,370
Let's make it a date
just for the two of us today, okay?

121
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,170
- We will be right back.
- All right, hurry back.

122
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:50,540
- You too, Ju Ni.
- Okay, Dad.

123
00:07:50,610 --> 00:07:53,540
Even if you miss me, hang in there.

124
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,680
I'll be back soon.

125
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:58,080
Yes, hurry back.

126
00:07:58,720 --> 00:07:59,720
Let's go.

127
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:16,300
Won't your dad get sulky?

128
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:20,570
Misfortune always strikes...

129
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:23,270
in the most cruel way
when least expected.

130
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:36,850
And it makes you endlessly obsess
and blame yourself.

131
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:48,270
If only I had listened to my daughter
and gone with them...

132
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,970
If only I had told them
not to walk...

133
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:05,350
I'll be there soon.

134
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:10,590
Daddy will be there soon.

135
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,560
That day, I...

136
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,030
was going to end my life.

137
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:18,560
A living man chasing after the dead?

138
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:25,500
It is none of your business, ma'am.

139
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:31,880
"Welcome, darling."
"I've been waiting for you, Dad."

140
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,380
"Thank you for dying after us."

141
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,650
Do you really think...

142
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,920
they would welcome you
with open arms?

143
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:50,090
What do you...

144
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,260
What do you know?

145
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,870
How could you possibly understand...

146
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,710
the pain of losing a child?

147
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:08,010
(Kim Hyun Jung, Cha Jun Sung)

148
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,250
That's my son.

149
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,990
My eldest child.

150
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:18,890
I want to follow my son too.

151
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:21,790
I want to do it this very second.

152
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,960
(Gong Hye Ji, Ju Ni)

153
00:10:26,230 --> 00:10:27,630
Let's live.

154
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:35,070
Let's keep living.

155
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,080
As we live on,

156
00:10:40,810 --> 00:10:43,210
we will find another reason
to keep going.

157
00:10:44,650 --> 00:10:45,720
I'm sure of it.

158
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,840
Thanks to Madam Chairwoman,

159
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,270
I'm here alive today.

160
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:10,110
I see.

161
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,450
See? What did I tell you?

162
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,310
I told you...

163
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,920
it was just an ordinary, dull story.

164
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:23,250
It is not ordinary at all.
Not in the slightest.

165
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:25,920
It must have been painful to bring up,

166
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:27,990
so thank you for sharing, Dr. Ju.

167
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:33,100
By the way,
how was the chicken soup?

168
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:35,530
Yes, it was truly delicious.

169
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:39,240
It was actually an acquaintance's mother
who ran that place.

170
00:11:40,170 --> 00:11:41,310
Is that so?

171
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,010
What a coincidence.

172
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:46,810
It's a place I'm very grateful for.

173
00:11:47,950 --> 00:11:49,010
Grateful?

174
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,280
Yes.

175
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:54,220
I truly am.

176
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:02,330
Dr. Ju, would you mind
if I head out first?

177
00:12:02,630 --> 00:12:04,330
I have someone to meet nearby.

178
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,660
Of course.

179
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,970
Thank you for coming to see me.

180
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:13,670
Please continue to take good care
of my grandmother.

181
00:12:14,410 --> 00:12:16,570
Of course. I will do my best.

182
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,020
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

183
00:12:28,950 --> 00:12:30,490
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

184
00:12:30,490 --> 00:12:31,660
Have you been waiting long?

185
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,230
No, I had some business
at the clinic,

186
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:36,630
and I just finished up.

187
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,070
Have you been crying?

188
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,770
No, why would I cry?

189
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,700
My eyes just get watery easily.

190
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:50,710
Anyway, what brings you here
to see me today?

191
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:56,080
It feels awkward to talk
standing here like this.

192
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,550
What? A personal assistant?

193
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,360
So you are saying
you want me to be Jaden Cha's...

194
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:09,490
I mean, you want me to be...

195
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:13,960
Designer Cha Seung Yun's
personal assistant right now?

196
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,970
I'm offering you the chance
to try it out, Kang Da Mi.

197
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:21,070
Why me?

198
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:24,710
Why offer it to me of all people?

199
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:28,310
Isn't it your dream
to become a fashion designer?

200
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,080
Yes, it is.

201
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:33,450
You majored in it in college,

202
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:35,350
and you have worked as a manager...

203
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:37,120
at a department store
VIP showroom, right?

204
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:39,490
That's true.

205
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,960
I think that makes you
plenty qualified...

206
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,290
to be my personal assistant.

207
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:47,530
Kang Da Mi, for starters,
I would like you as my assistant.

208
00:13:47,970 --> 00:13:49,030
Let's work together.

209
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,970
I appreciate the offer, but...

210
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,340
But what?

211
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:58,280
Aren't you working
as the head designer...

212
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,410
at Hwanggeum Apparel?

213
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,380
Yes, for the time being.

214
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:07,080
Well, I don't want to work
at Hwanggeum Apparel.

215
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:14,290
I heard you turned down
my brother's offer, so I know.

216
00:14:14,290 --> 00:14:15,390
But don't worry too much.

217
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:18,300
The one contracted to work
with Hwanggeum Apparel is me,

218
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:19,700
not you, Kang Da Mi.

219
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,430
What do you mean by that?

220
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,130
I'm a freelancer.

221
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:28,210
I pay my personal assistant
out of my own pocket.

222
00:14:28,670 --> 00:14:31,780
That means you won't be
on Hwanggeum Apparel's payroll.

223
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,740
Still, if I work for you...

224
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:37,080
I mean, if I work with you, sir...

225
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:38,650
If I end up doing that,

226
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:41,220
won't I have to commute...

227
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:43,950
to Hwanggeum Apparel
for the duration of the contract?

228
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:56,770
I thought you had that much guts.
Was I wrong?

229
00:14:58,970 --> 00:15:00,400
Guts?

230
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:03,670
Kang Da Mi, you know.

231
00:15:04,110 --> 00:15:06,610
I have always thought of you
as a pretty courageous person.

232
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:11,350
Ever since the first time
we met in the elevator, until now.

233
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:14,990
Right, back then...

234
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:19,620
I have a lot of work to do,
so I should get going first today.

235
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:21,690
Call me when you make up your mind.

236
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,960
Wait a minute.

237
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:25,060
Yes?

238
00:15:29,270 --> 00:15:30,670
How much will you pay me?

239
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,040
That's the most important thing
to me.

240
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:36,070
Let's see...

241
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:42,180
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

242
00:15:42,250 --> 00:15:43,650
What did you just say?

243
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,250
Mother is looking into someone?

244
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,290
Yes.

245
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,790
Why are you so surprised, though?

246
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:54,960
I was just...

247
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:57,490
wondering why she would do that.

248
00:15:57,560 --> 00:16:00,000
I was also a bit upset
that she gave the job to Dr. Ju,

249
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,130
so I asked her about it.

250
00:16:01,770 --> 00:16:04,770
She just said it was personal
and drew a line.

251
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,610
So it has nothing to do
with the company, then?

252
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,810
Yes, I guess not.

253
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:16,580
Do you really have no idea
who Mother is looking for?

254
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:21,120
You seem pretty curious.

255
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:23,290
Should I find a good time
to ask her again?

256
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:28,460
Mother is not in good health,
so given the situation,

257
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:31,200
I wonder who she is looking for
through Dr. Ju.

258
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,900
Honey.

259
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:37,030
Mother's health
always comes first to me.

260
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,200
You know that.

261
00:16:39,170 --> 00:16:42,510
Of course I do.
And I'm always grateful for it.

262
00:16:44,410 --> 00:16:45,540
Still,

263
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:48,150
I think Dr. Ju...

264
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:52,350
plays a much bigger role
in Mother's life than we thought.

265
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:56,290
He seems quite important to her.

266
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:02,290
(Product Planning Team Leader
Cha Do Yun)

267
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:06,760
I don't have any good memories
associated with Hwanggeum Apparel.

268
00:17:07,630 --> 00:17:08,670
Does this mean...

269
00:17:09,230 --> 00:17:10,770
we won't be seeing
each other anymore?

270
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:13,470
I suppose so.

271
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,570
Take care, Team Leader Cha.

272
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,010
Was that really the last time?

273
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,980
Why do I feel so disappointed?

274
00:17:39,930 --> 00:17:40,960
Excuse me, Team Leader Cha.

275
00:17:42,430 --> 00:17:43,470
Yes?

276
00:17:43,470 --> 00:17:45,670
You need to hire someone to run
the pop-up store.

277
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:50,440
We need to schedule interviews,
so please review the resumes...

278
00:17:50,510 --> 00:17:52,010
and select the candidates
for the second round.

279
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,940
I will contact them today.

280
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:57,580
All right. Let's do that.

281
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:14,430
Yes.

282
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:18,370
Did you two come down...

283
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,170
and receive the drink
Seung Yun offered you...

284
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:23,510
before leaving?

285
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:37,420
Right. If a past is too clean,

286
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:43,090
it could mean someone deliberately
wiped it clean.

287
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:46,530
Could it be...

288
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:53,400
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

289
00:18:58,710 --> 00:18:59,710
You...

290
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:03,150
should've talked to me first, Mom.

291
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:11,920
Then you shouldn't have
asked me how much I'd saved.

292
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:15,730
Did she?

293
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,260
No, that can't be.

294
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,970
What are you muttering
to yourself about?

295
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:26,000
Are you worried about Da Mi?

296
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,410
I heard she wasn't even that angry
when she left.

297
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:30,770
It would've been better
if she got mad.

298
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,380
She looked so heartbroken.

299
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:36,850
(Shipping Invoice)

300
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:39,020
(Customer Kang Dae Chi)

301
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:41,450
- Hello?
- You finally answered,

302
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:42,920
Mr. Kang Dae Chi.

303
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:46,520
Have you been
doing well all this time?

304
00:19:49,130 --> 00:19:51,060
I was actually about to call you.

305
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:55,200
Listen.
Something very urgent came up,

306
00:19:55,270 --> 00:19:57,870
- so next week...
- Where are you right now...

307
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,700
that you're whispering like that?

308
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:02,770
Are you really at the office?

309
00:20:03,510 --> 00:20:06,280
Of course I'm.
Where else would I be at this hour?

310
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,110
And besides,
whether I whisper or yell,

311
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:12,950
I don't think that's
any of your business.

312
00:20:13,150 --> 00:20:15,650
So you really are at work.

313
00:20:15,950 --> 00:20:18,290
Understood, sir.

314
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:22,060
I was just so worried about you...

315
00:20:22,130 --> 00:20:24,960
that I wanted to check in,
so please don't get the wrong idea.

316
00:20:25,730 --> 00:20:28,530
I'll see you very soon, then.

317
00:20:28,730 --> 00:20:30,930
Hang in there today,
Mr. Kang Dae Chi.

318
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:41,080
So you're going to lie to me?

319
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,750
Time to roll out.

320
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:48,290
Who is this kid?

321
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,890
She gets under my skin
in a whole new way.

322
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:57,290
Even if I write an explanation
and turn it in,

323
00:20:57,660 --> 00:20:59,200
I need to avoid disciplinary action.

324
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:03,000
If I'm unlucky enough
to get fired...

325
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,840
Darn it.

326
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,640
Seriously.

327
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,710
Right. At least seeing
you suffer like this...

328
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:19,250
proves you're human, Dae Chi.

329
00:21:20,550 --> 00:21:21,550
Hey.

330
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:24,120
- Are you done talking?
- No.

331
00:21:24,190 --> 00:21:26,690
Right now, I have a million things
I want to hold against you,

332
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,560
and I'm barely holding myself back.

333
00:21:29,490 --> 00:21:31,090
So unless you want
your hair ripped out,

334
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,430
don't mess with me.

335
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,530
Are you taking your anger out
on me...

336
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,170
just because Mom gave me
80,000 dollars? Is that it?

337
00:21:39,870 --> 00:21:41,810
Fine, since you brought it up,
let me talk.

338
00:21:43,570 --> 00:21:46,010
Did you really have to take
that money from her too?

339
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:49,650
Couldn't you put out the fire
with what I gave you?

340
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:52,180
Hey, that's just your take.

341
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:55,150
Can you even imagine how I feel
being in debt for 1,130,000 dollars?

342
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,590
She forced it into my hands
when I said no,

343
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:01,490
so how was I supposed
to turn it down in my situation?

344
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:05,460
The interest is snowballing
just while I breathe.

345
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:07,930
To you, that money is just
a measly 80,000 dollars, right?

346
00:22:08,830 --> 00:22:09,930
But that money...

347
00:22:11,230 --> 00:22:13,740
- That money...
- Money is money. So what?

348
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:16,440
Forget it.

349
00:22:17,970 --> 00:22:19,980
And I'm telling you one more time,

350
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:22,680
don't you dare tell Mom...

351
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:25,320
or anyone else in the family
that I gave you money.

352
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:28,050
- Got it?
- I got it.

353
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:33,460
- Why can't I tell them, anyway?
- If I say don't, just don't.

354
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:48,440
Everything else is fine,

355
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:51,640
but there are quite a lot of seniors
in this neighborhood in the morning.

356
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:53,540
Now I can finally catch my breath.

357
00:22:56,610 --> 00:23:00,320
Ouch, my back. My back hurts.

358
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:08,430
He set it up nice and clean.

359
00:23:08,830 --> 00:23:11,190
Welcome. Goodness!

360
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:16,730
Mother, what brings you here?

361
00:23:20,370 --> 00:23:25,040
How come there's
not a soul in sight here too?

362
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,920
What do I do?

363
00:23:34,450 --> 00:23:36,590
What do I do? I'm going crazy.

364
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:40,590
This is no way to live.

365
00:23:44,130 --> 00:23:46,130
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

366
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:50,730
Well, having the nerve
to be that brazen...

367
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:53,540
is how she could steal
another woman's husband. Indeed.

368
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,110
Mother, are you already done
with your appointment?

369
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:59,910
Why did you come out?

370
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,250
I was thinking
of seeing the doctor, too.

371
00:24:02,750 --> 00:24:04,980
I have a headache
and feel congested.

372
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:07,550
It's nothing for you
to worry about, though.

373
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:09,620
Did you stop by
the pharmacy already?

374
00:24:10,290 --> 00:24:12,560
What? No.

375
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:14,930
Pardon?

376
00:24:16,090 --> 00:24:17,090
Don't...

377
00:24:17,590 --> 00:24:18,860
go to the clinic.

378
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:21,670
Why?

379
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:23,800
Well, over there...

380
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:26,270
Right, there's no one there.

381
00:24:27,370 --> 00:24:28,540
Is Dr. Ju not in?

382
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:30,610
It looked like they were open.

383
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:31,980
What are you standing around for?

384
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,510
I told you no one is there,
so hurry up and go inside.

385
00:24:34,580 --> 00:24:36,950
Yes. Let's go in, Mother.

386
00:24:37,010 --> 00:24:38,950
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

387
00:24:42,190 --> 00:24:44,190
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

388
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:53,360
Why does she walk through this alley
every day to commute?

389
00:24:54,030 --> 00:24:55,500
My heart is pounding.

390
00:24:56,430 --> 00:24:58,030
I need to make her quit
before she gets caught...

391
00:24:58,540 --> 00:25:00,900
and bring her home today.

392
00:25:04,510 --> 00:25:06,680
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

393
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:16,620
My dear granddaughter.
You're early today.

394
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:20,160
The library is showing
a free movie today, Grandma.

395
00:25:20,220 --> 00:25:22,330
Dad and I are going to see it
together later.

396
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:24,260
By the way...

397
00:25:24,530 --> 00:25:26,500
Auntie Ri Ja, seriously.

398
00:25:28,670 --> 00:25:30,530
- What's wrong?
- Mom,

399
00:25:30,930 --> 00:25:34,100
giving only Dae Chi money
caused this whole mess.

400
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:35,910
You should've treated us equally,

401
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,740
or not given anything at all.

402
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,610
Now Da Mi is getting
scolded for nothing.

403
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:43,350
- By who?
- Who do you think?

404
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:48,290
Just leave it be.

405
00:25:48,990 --> 00:25:51,520
It's not like Da Mi
will just sit there and take it.

406
00:25:51,690 --> 00:25:53,960
- Still...
- Come on.

407
00:25:54,790 --> 00:25:59,130
If you go up there right now,
it'll turn into a real family fight.

408
00:26:06,370 --> 00:26:08,540
Why can't you answer me?

409
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:11,780
Even if my sister
steadily saved up in that account...

410
00:26:11,780 --> 00:26:13,440
with the intention
of giving it to you,

411
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:16,050
I'm asking if that money is yours.

412
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:17,850
Did you save that money yourself?

413
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:21,020
I never said it was mine.

414
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:24,960
Then just because
my sister dipped into it...

415
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:26,320
for a moment
to help out her own son,

416
00:26:26,560 --> 00:26:27,760
why are you pouting,

417
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:30,360
stomping around,
and sulking in this house?

418
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:33,800
Frankly speaking,
whether she gives it to you,

419
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:37,070
burns it, or throws it away,
it is none of your business.

420
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:40,500
How can it not be my business?
I'm her daughter.

421
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,710
Auntie, it's not that
I'm upset and angry...

422
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:46,880
because Mom gave Dae Chi
the money meant for me...

423
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:48,040
without saying a word.

424
00:26:48,650 --> 00:26:52,150
It's just that I know
how hard and how long Mom worked...

425
00:26:52,450 --> 00:26:54,750
to save that money for me,

426
00:26:54,750 --> 00:26:57,350
- and that is why...
- So, if you know that,

427
00:26:57,350 --> 00:26:59,290
shouldn't you just be grateful?

428
00:27:00,490 --> 00:27:02,590
Then can't I even
be upset in this house?

429
00:27:03,060 --> 00:27:04,460
Am I not even allowed to get angry?

430
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:07,730
You can do that
with the other family members.

431
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:10,700
You tease me and snap at me
from time to time too,

432
00:27:10,830 --> 00:27:12,400
and you give your brothers attitude.

433
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:16,110
But at least in this house,
you must never do that to Mrs. Choi,

434
00:27:16,540 --> 00:27:20,080
especially to your mother,
who is my sister.

435
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:22,880
Why?

436
00:27:23,380 --> 00:27:24,680
Why can't I do that?

437
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:28,720
Girl, do I really have to
spell it out for you?

438
00:27:31,390 --> 00:27:32,860
Maybe when you were
young and foolish, sure,

439
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:35,690
but if you appreciate how my sister
took you in and raised you,

440
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:37,930
you should behave yourself by now.

441
00:27:38,190 --> 00:27:40,060
Stop upsetting my sister.

442
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:42,430
Aunt Ri Ja.

443
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:44,170
What? What is it?

444
00:27:46,270 --> 00:27:47,470
Can't you keep your mouth shut?

445
00:28:06,890 --> 00:28:08,760
(Mission: Mompossible)

446
00:28:08,830 --> 00:28:11,430
I raised my own child.
Why feel bad or pity for me?

447
00:28:11,430 --> 00:28:13,000
After raising her well
all this time,

448
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:15,130
shouldn't you get to lean
on her a little now?

449
00:28:15,530 --> 00:28:17,200
Never let me see your face again.

450
00:28:17,470 --> 00:28:19,640
And stay far away from Mi Mi.

451
00:28:19,700 --> 00:28:20,770
Mom, I'm home.

452
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:23,210
Who are you?

453
00:28:23,470 --> 00:28:25,810
I think it'd be best
if you moved out.

454
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:29,250
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
